  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training Indonesian Farmers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The long term grassroot level activities in Sumatra and Java to integrate climate change mitigation with poverty reduction through restoration of degraded land into productive food forests, participating farmer groups have recently requested CO2 Operate B.V. to help them to access (inter)national markets. For this, the quality (international standards) and quantity (enough and regular supply) of their products must improve. Training of the farmer groups and the  trading partner GER Indonesia  in post harvesting and trading for export area will be crucial components to make this step.The project has taken place on two different islands, namely Sumatra and java. However, by far the most work will take place in Solok and Agam district, West Sumatra. Here the  focus has been on essential oil production and coffee production. The arenga palm sugar activities have taken place in West Java (the area of Cisolok). With the DGGF-TA funding the training of a 177 people, including 170 farmers has been realised in order to make them &#x201c;export-ready&#x201d;. Strengthening the (internal) management systems of the trading partner GER Indonesia has enabled more effective collaboration for exporting of products.</narrative>
  </description>
